From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DeepSeek V4.1 DSpark: no pre-collapse MTP hidden-state buffer

DeepseekV4Model allocated a [max_num_batched_tokens, hc_mult * hidden]
buffer for every eagle-family drafter, DSpark included, and filled it every
step that does not run prefill sequence parallelism: a full-row scatter of
the CED decoder's rows and a copy (each long prefill chunk's CED boundary
ends SP, so those chunks wrote it too). The runner hands it to the drafter
as last_hidden_states through get_mtp_target_hidden_states, but the DSpark
speculator drafts from the target's aux hidden states and its own
draft-hidden context buffer; it reads last_hidden_states only when there
are no aux hidden states, which DSpark always has. DSpark now gets no buffer,
get_mtp_target_hidden_states returns None, and the runner then passes the
target's hidden states, as for a target without the hook. The target's
computation is unchanged (the buffer was written from states the final
collapse also reads, and without SP the write gathered nothing), and DSpark
never read the buffer, so outputs are unchanged. With no DSpark buffer to
skip, prefill_sp_skips_mtp_buffer goes.

The native model, its CED compaction and prefill sequence parallelism are
Local Inference Lab's (Luke Alonso) and Christopher Owen's (spark-ds41f)
code. No upstream code is ported.

License: Apache-2.0 (dsv41-1017 recipe, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-4x-DGX-Spark).
